# Docker build-context exclusions.
#
# WHY THIS FILE MATTERS MORE THAN IT LOOKS: without it, `docker build` sends the
# whole working tree, and the Dockerfiles' `COPY apps/api apps/api` /
# `COPY packages/db packages/db` then copy it into the image. Two concrete
# consequences, both verified by building:
#
#  1. SECRETS. apps/api/.env, apps/api-python/.env and infra/staging/staging.env
#     hold DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET, OPENAI_API_KEY and INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKEN.
#     They are correctly gitignored and have never been committed — but .gitignore
#     has no bearing on a Docker build context, so every image was being built with
#     those files baked into a layer, readable by anyone who can pull the image.
#     The env-var discipline in the Dockerfiles is pointless while this is true.
#
#  2. THE BUILD ACTUALLY BREAKS. The host's node_modules (built on the developer's
#     OS, full of symlinks and native binaries) was copied over the Linux
#     dependencies installed in the `deps` stage, so `prisma generate` failed with
#     "Cannot find module /repo/packages/db/node_modules/prisma/build/index.js".
#     No image built at all until this file existed.
#
# Keep the ignore list ahead of the Dockerfiles' COPY lines: anything genuinely
# needed at build time must NOT be listed here.

# --- Dependencies: always reinstalled inside the image, never copied in -------
node_modules
**/node_modules

# --- Secrets and local configuration ------------------------------------------
# Deliberately broad. The .example templates are re-included below because the
# images do not need them, but excluding a template by accident is harmless
# while including a real secret by accident is not.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
infra/staging/staging.env
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# --- Build output: regenerated inside the image -------------------------------
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo
.pnpm-store

# --- Local runtime state -------------------------------------------------------
.local-storage
coverage
**/coverage
*.log

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.venv
.venv-ci

# --- VCS, tooling and docs: nothing at build time reads these -------------------
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
docs
load-tests
*.md
audit_raw.json
audit_script.js
